@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "provisioning.license.integration"

Feature: Koroneiki To Provisioning License API
	Testing Provisioning License API functionality.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the product consumption list on koroneiki made by the account "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production                   |
	| DXP Non-Production               |
	| Portal Production                |
	| DXP Development                  |
	| Commerce Subscription Production |
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP OEM                                         |
	| DXP Limited                                     |
	| DXP Non-Production                              |
	| Portal Per User                                 |
	| Commerce Subscription Development               |
	| Commerce Subscription Non-Production            |
	| Commerce Subscription Backup                    |
	| Commerce Subscription Unlimited Enterprise-Wide |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| KORLICKORLIC |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| KORLICKORLIC |
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: Deactivate and activate new DXP license
	Testing the ability to deactivate and activate licenses via API.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORLICKORLIC                         | |
	| Contact Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}        | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Profile Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         | |
	And I generate the account key value for "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I generate future static start and end dates
	And I generate future static full start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" for "DXP Production"
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticKoroneikiAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticKoroneikiAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the license index page
	And I click on the generate license button on the license index
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Account | Select Entity | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | Select        | DXP Production                | |
	| Version | Select        | 7.2                           | |
	| Type    | Select        | DXP Production                | |
	And I click on the choose button for the product purchase in position "1" on the license form
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Host Name     | Input    | localhost         | |
	| IP Addresses  | Textarea | 123.45.67.89      | |
	| MAC Addresses | Textarea | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F | |
	And I click on the generate button on the license form
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header  | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | DXP Production                | |
	When I go to the license index page
	And I search the licenses page using the keyword "${staticAccountKey}"
	Then I should be able to view a license on the provisioning index with the keyword "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name          | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Description   | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Account       | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Product       | DXP Production                 |
	| Type          | Production                     |
	| Details       | Host Name: localhost           |
	| Details       | IP Address: 123.45.67.89       |
	| Details       | MAC Address: 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F |
	| Status        | ACTIVE                         |
	| Complimentary | false                          |
	When I deactivate the license on provisioning with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the account "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I search the licenses page using the keyword "${staticAccountKey}"
	Then I should be able to view a license on the provisioning index with the keyword "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name          | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Description   | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Account       | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Product       | DXP Production                 |
	| Type          | Production                     |
	| Details       | Host Name: localhost           |
	| Details       | IP Address: 123.45.67.89       |
	| Details       | MAC Address: 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F |
	| Status        | DEACTIVATED                    |
	| Complimentary | false                          |
	When I activate the license on provisioning with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the account "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I search the licenses page using the keyword "${staticAccountKey}"
	Then I should be able to view a license on the provisioning index with the keyword "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name          | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Description   | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Account       | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Product       | DXP Production                 |
	| Type          | Production                     |
	| Details       | Host Name: localhost           |
	| Details       | IP Address: 123.45.67.89       |
	| Details       | MAC Address: 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F |
	| Status        | ACTIVE                         |
	| Complimentary | false                          |

Scenario: View active and deactivated licenses
	Testing the ability to view active and deactivated licenses via API.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORLICKORLIC                         | |
	| Contact Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}        | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Profile Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         | |
	And I generate the account key value for "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I generate future static start and end dates
	And I generate future static full start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" for "DXP Production"
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticKoroneikiAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticKoroneikiAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the license index page
	And I click on the generate license button on the license index
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Account | Select Entity | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | Select        | DXP Production                | |
	| Version | Select        | 7.2                           | |
	| Type    | Select        | DXP Production                | |
	And I click on the choose button for the product purchase in position "1" on the license form
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Name          | Input    | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License1 Name        | |
	| Description   | Input    | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License1 Description | |
	| Host Name     | Input    | localhost                                          | |
	| IP Addresses  | Textarea | 123.45.67.89                                       | |
	| MAC Addresses | Textarea | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F                                  | |
	And I click on the generate button on the license form
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header  | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | DXP Production                | |
	When I go to the license index page
	And I click on the generate license button on the license index
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Account | Select Entity | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | Select        | DXP Production                | |
	| Version | Select        | 7.2                           | |
	| Type    | Select        | DXP Production                | |
	And I click on the choose button for the product purchase in position "1" on the license form
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Name          | Input    | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License2 Name        | |
	| Description   | Input    | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License2 Description | |
	| Host Name     | Input    | localhost                                          | |
	| IP Addresses  | Textarea | 123.45.67.89                                       | |
	| MAC Addresses | Textarea | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F                                  | |
	And I click on the generate button on the license form
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header  | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | DXP Production                | |
	And I should be able to view the active license on the account "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License1 Name" and the following values
	| Name               | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License1 Name |
	| License Entry Type | Production                                  |
	And I should be able to view the active license on the account "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License2 Name" and the following values
	| Name               | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License2 Name |
	| License Entry Type | Production                                  |
	And I should not be able to view the deactivated license on the account "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License1 Name"
	And I should not be able to view the deactivated license on the account "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License2 Name"
	When I go to the license index page
	And I search the licenses page using the keyword "${staticAccountKey}"
	And I click on the license with the keyword "Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License1 Name" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the deactivate button for the license in position "1" on the license page
	Then I should be able to view the deactivated license on the account "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License1 Name" and the following values
	| Name | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License1 Name |
	And I should be able to view the active license on the account "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License2 Name" and the following values
	| Name | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License2 Name |
	And I should not be able to view the active license on the account "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License1 Name"
	And I should not be able to view the deactivated license on the account "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License2 Name"

Scenario: Extend new DXP license
	Testing the ability to extend new DXP license via API.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORLICKORLIC                         | |
	| Contact Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}        | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Profile Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         | |
	And I generate the account key value for "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I generate static full non abbreviated start and end dates
	And I generate future static start and end dates
	And I generate future static full start and end dates
	And I generate future static full non abbreviated start and end dates
	And I generate future static yyyymmdd start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I generate the product purchase key value for the product purchase made by "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" for "DXP Production"
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticKoroneikiAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticKoroneikiAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the license index page
	And I click on the generate license button on the license index
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Account | Select Entity | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}    | |
	| Product | Select        | DXP Production                   | |
	| Version | Select        | 7.2                              | |
	| Type    | Select        | DXP Production (Virtual Cluster) | |
	And I click on the choose button for the product purchase in position "1" on the license form
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Maximum Cluster Nodes | Input | 5 | |
	And I click on the generate button on the license form
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header  | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | DXP Production                | |
	When I go to the license index page
	And I search the licenses page using the keyword "${staticAccountKey}"
	Then I should be able to view a license on the provisioning index with the keyword "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name          | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Description   | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Account       | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product       | DXP Production                |
	| Type          | Virtual Cluster               |
	| Details       | Maximum Cluster Nodes: 5      |
	| Status        | ACTIVE                        |
	| Complimentary | false                         |
	When I click on the license with the keyword "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header                | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product               | DXP Production                | |
	| Version               | 7.2                           | |
	| Type                  | Virtual Cluster               | |
	| Owner                 | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Description           | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Maximum Cluster Nodes | 5                             | |
	| Complimentary         | No                            | |
	| Status                | ACTIVE                        | |
	| Created By            | Test Test                     | |
	When I go to the license index page
	And I search the licenses page using the keyword "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}"
	When I click on the license with the keyword "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header               | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product              | DXP Production                | |
	| Version              | 7.2                           | |
	| Type                 | Virtual Cluster               | |
	| Owner                | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Description          | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Maximum Cluster Nodes| 5                             | |
	| Complimentary        | No                            | |
	| Status               | ACTIVE                        | |
	| Created By           | Test Test                     | |
	When I obtain the license key ID value from the license details page
	And I extend the license on provisioning with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the account "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the product purchase key "${staticProductPurchaseKey}" with the following values
	| Start Date      | ${staticFutureStartDate} |
	| Expiration Date | ${staticFutureEndDate}   |
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header               | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product              | DXP Production                | |
	| Version              | 7.2                           | |
	| Type                 | Virtual Cluster               | |
	| Owner                | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Description          | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Maximum Cluster Nodes| 5                             | |
	| Complimentary        | No                            | |
	| Status               | ACTIVE                        | |
	| Created By           | Test Test                     | |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korlic"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the product with the name "DXP Production" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name                | DXP Production |
	| Current Provisioned | 10             |
	| State               | ACTIVE         |
	When I click on the "Licenses" tab
	Then I should be able to view the license with the keyword "${staticFullNonAbbreviatedFutureEndDate}" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name            | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}            |
	| Description     | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}            |
	| Expiration Date | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedFutureEndDate} |
	| Type            | Virtual Cluster                          |
	| Product         | DXP Production                           |
	| Details         | Maximum Cluster Nodes: 5                 |
	| Status          | ACTIVE                                   |
	| Complimentary   | false                                    |
	And I should be able to view the license with the keyword "${staticFullNonAbbreviatedEndDate}" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name            | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}                    |
	| Description     | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}                    |
	| Expiration Date | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedEndDate}               |
	| Product         | DXP Production                                   |
	| Type            | Virtual Cluster                                  |
	| Details         | Maximum Cluster Nodes: 5                         |
	| Status          | ACTIVE                                           |
	| Complimentary   | false                                            |
	And the "Active" license tab should have the count value "2"
	And the "Expired" license tab should have the count value "0"
	And the "Deactivated" license tab should have the count value "0"
	And the "All" license tab should have the count value "2"
	When I click on the "Expired" license tab
	Then I should not be able to view the license with the keyword "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the account details page
	When I click on the "Deactivated" license tab
	Then I should not be able to view the license with the keyword "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the account details page
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korlic"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "DXP Production" subscription link
	And I click on the "Licenses" tab
	Then I should be able to view the license with the keyword "${staticFullNonAbbreviatedFutureEndDate}" and the following values on the subscription details page
	| Name            | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}            |
	| Description     | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}            |
	| Expiration Date | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedFutureEndDate} |
	| Type            | Virtual Cluster                          |
	| Product         | DXP Production                           |
	| Details         | Maximum Cluster Nodes: 5                 |
	| Status          | ACTIVE                                   |
	| Complimentary   | false                                    |
	And I should be able to view the license with the keyword "${staticFullNonAbbreviatedEndDate}" and the following values on the subscription details page
	| Name            | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}                    |
	| Description     | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}                    |
	| Expiration Date | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedEndDate}               |
	| Product         | DXP Production                                   |
	| Type            | Virtual Cluster                                  |
	| Details         | Maximum Cluster Nodes: 5                         |
	| Status          | ACTIVE                                           |
	| Complimentary   | false                                            |
	And the "Active" license tab should have the count value "2"
	And the "Expired" license tab should have the count value "0"
	And the "Deactivated" license tab should have the count value "0"
	And the "All" license tab should have the count value "2"
	When I click on the "Expired" license tab
	Then I should not be able to view the license with the keyword "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the subscription details page
	When I click on the "Deactivated" license tab
	Then I should not be able to view the license with the keyword "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the subscription details page

